WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
My entire life, I never had a real say about any of it.

2
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.000
This last one, cancer...

3
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.500
All I have left is how I choose to approach this.

4
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.000
A substantial amount of methamphetamine being taken off the street.

5
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.700
Hey, how much money is that?

6
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.000
It's about 700 grand.

7
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.480
It's a pretty good haul.

8
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:31.240
Just say the word and I'll take you on a ride-along.

9
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.440
Get a little excitement in your life.

10
00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:35.440
Someday.

11
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:50.000
[Music]

12
00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:53.800
The DEA took all your money, your lab...

13
00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.600
But you know the business.

14
00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.800
And I know the chemistry.

15
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:02.400
You want to cook crystal meth?

16
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:05.320
You?

17
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.600
I get it now. You want to make some cash for your people before you check out.

18
00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:10.680
You got a problem with that?

19
00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.040
I'm your partner, man. You should've told me.

20
00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:19.160
You're coming home so late, and we're just left wondering where you were.

21
00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:25.000
We got new players. Now, we don't know who they are, where they come from.

22
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.500
Albuquerque just might have a new kingpin.

23
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:36.500
It is the purest, most chemically sound product on the market. Anywhere.

24
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.500
How much product do you have?

25
00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:46.000
You are not how I remember you from class. I mean, like, not at all.

26
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.000
What?

27
00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.000
There is no room for error.

28
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.000
Not with these people.

29
00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:57.000
What does a man do?

30
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:04.000
A man provides for his family.

31
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.000
It's cost my family.

32
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.000
How many people are gonna die because of us?

33
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.000
We're in control. No one gets hurt.

34
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.000
There will be plenty of time for soul-searching.

35
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.000
Until then...

36
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.000
We have to cook.

37
00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.000
What I want...

38
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.000
What I need...

39
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.000
...is a choice.

40
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.000
Then make the right choice.
